#. i18n: ectx: whatsthis, entry (ShowAddressAction), group (Show Address Settings)
#. +> future stable
#: actions/contactactionssettings.kcfg.cmake:17
msgid "Defines which application shall be used to show the postal address of a contact on a map. If 'Web Browser' is selected, an URL can be defined with placeholders for the single address parts. If 'External Application' is selected, a command with placeholders can be defined."
msgstr "Fastleggen, mit wat för en Programm en Kontakt sien Postadress op de Koort wiest warrt. Is »Nettkieker« utsöcht, lett sik en URL mit Platzhollers för enkelte Adressdelen fastleggen. Is »Extern Programm« utsöcht, lett sik en Befehl mit Platzhollers fastleggen."

#. i18n: ectx: whatsthis, entry (AddressUrl), group (Show Address Settings)
#. +> future stable
#: actions/contactactionssettings.kcfg.cmake:22
msgid "This URL defines the website that shall be used to show a contact's postal address."
msgstr "Disse Adress leggt de Nettsiet fast, op de en Kontakt sien Postadress wiest warrt."

#. i18n: ectx: tooltip, entry (AddressUrl), group (Show Address Settings)
#. +> future stable
#: actions/contactactionssettings.kcfg.cmake:28
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following placeholders can be used in the URL:\n"
"   %s: Street\n"
"   %r: Region\n"
"   %l: Location\n"
"   %z: Zip Code\n"
"   %c: Country ISO Code"
msgstr ""
"De URL ünnerstütt disse Platzhollers:\n"
"   %s: Straat\n"
"   %r: Regioon\n"
"   %l: Oort\n"
"   %z: Postleddtall\n"
"   %c: ISO-Lännerafkörten"

#. i18n: ectx: label, entry (AddressCommand), group (Show Address Settings)
#. +> future stable
#: actions/contactactionssettings.kcfg.cmake:31
msgid "Address Command"
msgstr "Adressbefehl"

#. i18n: ectx: whatsthis, entry (AddressCommand), group (Show Address Settings)
#. +> future stable
#: actions/contactactionssettings.kcfg.cmake:32
msgid "This command defines the application that shall be executed to show a contact's postal address."
msgstr "Disse Befehl leggt dat Programm fast, mit dat en Kontakt sien Postadress wiest warrt."

#. i18n: ectx: tooltip, entry (AddressCommand), group (Show Address Settings)
#. +> future stable
#: actions/contactactionssettings.kcfg.cmake:38
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following placeholders can be used in the command:\n"
"   %s: Street\n"
"   %r: Region\n"
"   %l: Location\n"
"   %z: Zip Code\n"
"   %c: Country ISO Code"
msgstr ""
"De Befehl ünnerstütt disse Platzhollers:\n"
"   %s: Straat\n"
"   %r: Regioon\n"
"   %l: Oort\n"
"   %z: Postleddtall\n"
"   %c: ISO-Lännerafkörten"

#. i18n: ectx: whatsthis, entry (DialPhoneNumberAction), group (Phone Dial Settings)
#. +> future stable
#: actions/contactactionssettings.kcfg.cmake:51
msgid "Defines which application shall be used to dial the phone number of a contact. If 'Skype' is selected the Skype application will be started (if installed on the computer) and the number is dialed. If 'External Application' is selected, a command with placeholders can be defined."
msgstr "Fastleggen, mit wat för en Programm en Kontakt sien Telefoonnummer anropen warrt. Is »Skype« utsöcht, warrt Skype start (wenn dat op den Reekner installeert is), un de Nummer anwählt. Is »Extern Programm« utsöcht, lett sik en Befehl mit Platzhollers fastleggen."

#. i18n: ectx: label, entry (PhoneCommand), group (Phone Dial Settings)
#. +> future stable
#: actions/contactactionssettings.kcfg.cmake:55
msgid "Phone Command"
msgstr "Anroopbefehl"

#. i18n: ectx: whatsthis, entry (PhoneCommand), group (Phone Dial Settings)
#. +> future stable
#: actions/contactactionssettings.kcfg.cmake:56
msgid "This command defines the application that shall be executed to dial a contact's phone number."
msgstr "Disse Befehl leggt dat Programm fast, mit dat en Kontakt sien Telefoonnummer anropen warrt."

#. i18n: ectx: tooltip, entry (PhoneCommand), group (Phone Dial Settings)
#. +> future stable
#: actions/contactactionssettings.kcfg.cmake:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following placeholders can be used in the command:\n"
"   %N: The raw number as stored in the address book.\n"
"   %n: The normalized number with all non-digit characters removed."
msgstr ""
"De Befehl ünnerstütt disse Platzhollers:\n"
"   %N: De Nummer, so as se in't Adressbook sekert is.\n"
"   %n: De topasst Nummer, ahn Tekens, de keen Tallen sünd."

#. i18n: ectx: whatsthis, entry (SendSmsAction), group (Send SMS Settings)
#. +> future stable
#: actions/contactactionssettings.kcfg.cmake:71
msgid "Defines which application shall be used to send an SMS to the phone number of a contact. If 'Skype' is selected the Skype application will be started (if installed on the computer) and the SMS is sent via Skype. If 'External Application' is selected, a command with placeholders can be defined."
msgstr "Fastleggen, mit wat för en Programm en Kontakt sien Telefoonnummer en SMS tostüert warrt. Is »Skype« utsöcht, warrt Skype start (wenn dat op den Reekner installeert is), un de SMS över Skype loosstüert. Is »Extern Programm« utsöcht, lett sik en Befehl mit Platzhollers fastleggen."

#. i18n: ectx: label, entry (SmsCommand), group (Send SMS Settings)
#. +> future stable
#: actions/contactactionssettings.kcfg.cmake:75
msgid "SMS Command"
msgstr "SMS-Befehl"

#. i18n: ectx: whatsthis, entry (SmsCommand), group (Send SMS Settings)
#. +> future stable
#: actions/contactactionssettings.kcfg.cmake:76
msgid "This command defines the application that shall be executed to send an SMS to a contact's phone number."
msgstr "Disse Befehl leggt dat Programm fast, mit dat en Kontakt sien Telefoonnummer en SMS tostüert warrt."

#. i18n: ectx: tooltip, entry (SmsCommand), group (Send SMS Settings)
#. +> future stable
#: actions/contactactionssettings.kcfg.cmake:80
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following placeholders can be used in the command:\n"
"   %N: The raw number as stored in the address book.\n"
"   %n: The normalized number with all non-digit characters removed.\n"
"   %t: The text"
msgstr ""
"De Befehl ünnerstütt disse Platzhollers:\n"
"   %N: De Nummer, so as se in't Adressbook sekert is.\n"
"   %n: De topasst Nummer, ahn Tekens, de keen Tallen sünd.\n"
"   %t: De Text"

